@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+# Observability: logging & ops alerting
+
+Everything the application emits at runtime falls into exactly **three lanes**.
+Pick the lane by asking one question: *who is supposed to act on this?*
+
+| Lane | Channel / mechanism | Destination | Retention | Audience |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **Archive** | `Log::debug()`…`Log::error()` (default `stack` → `daily`) | `storage/logs/laravel.log` (daily rotation) | 14 days (`LOG_DAILY_DAYS`) | Developers debugging an issue |
+| **Audit** | `Log::channel('audit')->info(…)` | `storage/logs/audit.log` (daily rotation) | 90 days (`LOG_AUDIT_DAYS`) | Anyone answering "who changed what / who tried what" |
+| **Alert** | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send(…)` | Discord incoming webhook | n/a (Discord) | Ops — a human who must act now |
+
+## Decision guide
+
+Use this quick check (also for AI agents touching the codebase):
+
+1. **Would a human need to be woken up right now?** → **Alert**.
+   A job that exhausted its retries, a payment-gateway webhook failing,
+   a plan limit blocking an entity. Call `DiscordOpsAlert` explicitly.
+2. **Is it a durable record of a business/security event?** → **Audit**.
+   Membership role changes, subscription transitions, payment state changes,
+   login lockouts, permission denials. Write to the `audit` channel.
+3. **Everything else** → **Archive**. Routine debug/info/warning/error logs
+   via the default `Log` facade (or `Log::channel('daily')` explicitly).
+
+Rules of thumb:
+
+- **Discord is never a Monolog channel.** There is deliberately no `discord`
+  channel in `config/logging.php`. Alerting is an *explicit call* made by code
+  that decided an incident is worth paging — not a side effect of logging.
+- **Audit is append-only and long-lived.** Never write routine noise there
+  (it would drown real events and waste 90-day storage), and never *not* write
+  a security/currency-relevant transition there because "it's also in the
+  archive log".
+- **Alerts are rare.** If you find yourself alerting more than a handful of
+  times a week, fix the underlying problem or demote to archive/audit.
+
+## Archive lane (default `daily`)
+
+```php
+Log::info('Queue rehashed', ['queue' => 'asaas-webhooks']);
+```
+
+- Default channel is `stack` (`LOG_CHANNEL`), which fans out to `daily`
+  (`LOG_STACK=daily`) — `storage/logs/laravel.log`, rotated daily,
+  kept 14 days (`LOG_DAILY_DAYS`).
+- Level defaults to `debug` (`LOG_LEVEL`); `daily` writes debug and up.
+
+## Audit lane (`audit`)
+
+```php
+Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [
+    'subscription_id' => $subscription->id,
+    'from' => 'active',
+    'to' => 'past_due',
+    'actor_user_id' => $user->id,
+]);
+```
+
+- Driver `daily`, file `storage/logs/audit.log`, kept 90 days
+  (`LOG_AUDIT_DAYS`), minimum level `info` (`LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL`).
+- Include *what changed*, *old → new value* and *who did it* (user id, IP,
+  guard) in the context array. Context is indexed and greppable — prefer it
+  over interpolating values into the message string.
+- Typical events: role/membership changes, subscription transitions, payment
+  record mutations, login lockouts, API key issuance/revocation.
+
+## Alert lane (`DiscordOpsAlert`)
+
+```php
+app(DiscordOpsAlert::class)->send(
+    'Payment webhook failing',
+    'Asaas webhook handler exhausted retries.',
+    ['webhook_id' => $webhook->id, 'attempts' => 5, 'queue' => 'asaas-webhooks'],
+);
+```
+
+Or inject `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert` and call `->send($title, $message, $context)`.
+
+- Config: `services.discord.webhook_url` ← env `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`.
+  **Unset/empty ⇒ silent no-op** (no HTTP request) — safe in local dev and CI.
+- The alert text is `title`, `message`, then one `key=value` line per context
+  entry, truncated to 1800 chars (Discord's hard limit is 2000).
+- Context values are redacted before sending: sensitive keys (`password`,
+  `token`, `secret`, `authorization`, `api_key`/`api-key`/`apikey`, `webhook`)
+  and any string containing a bearer credential become `[redacted]`; nested
+  arrays are redacted recursively and rendered as JSON.
+- **Soft-fail**: `send()` never throws. A non-2xx response or a transport
+  error (timeout, connection reset) is written to the archive log at `error`
+  level — with the webhook URL scrubbed, since it embeds the webhook token.
+- Alerting is fire-and-forget: no retries, no mention/role handling, no rate
+  limiting. If Discord is down, the incident log line is all you get.
+
+### When to send an alert
+
+- A queued job failed permanently (retries exhausted).
+- An inbound payment-provider webhook (e.g. Asaas) can't be processed.
+- A hard business limit blocks an entity (e.g. plan limit reached for a
+  critical flow).
+- Anything on-call would consider "stop the line".
+
+Do **not** alert for: user errors, validation failures, expected 4xx traffic,
+or anything already covered by audit logging alone.
+
+## Environment keys
+
+| Key | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `LOG_CHANNEL` | `stack` | Default channel |
+| `LOG_STACK` | `daily` | Channels the default `stack` fans out to |
+| `LOG_LEVEL` | `debug` | Minimum level for archive channels |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | `14` | Retention of the archive (`daily`) channel |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | `info` | Minimum level for the `audit` channel |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | `90` | Retention of the `audit` channel |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | *(empty)* | Ops alert webhook; empty disables alerting |
